#Server Architecture Design document 

##Introduction and overview 

As per the team and project plan the Central Control Tier is outlined below: 

Tier 3: Central Control Tier (Control-com) 
- Acts as the command centre, receiving the much lighter processed data from tier 2, and sending control action requests back down the hierarchy. 
- Manages the dynamic connection/disconnection of the µ-com. 

This document will not detail how the south or northbound APIs should work, instead focusing on how the server handles requests sent from both APIs.  

##Design structure 

###Resource usage 
- Should be efficient to allow for us to run the process on the lab computer or alongside the machine vision system aboard the raspberry pi 

###Data Handling 

####Should hold on to some values in memory  
- Current set point  
- Current deviation  

####Stretch goals for permanent storage 
- Prior set points 
- Prior Deviations 

##Data design 
- will store data in the same format as the north and southbound API
- .Json, works best with RESTful APIs

##Project Assumptions 
- All communication outside the main server process should be done via APIs 

##Language, Tools and Libraries Used 
- All server language should be done in rust  
- Data that is being passed through the server should reflect that outlined in the API design docs  
